  "do_113569878939262976132": {
    "id": "do_113569878939262976132",
    "name": "Prevention of Sexual Harassment of Women at Workplace",
    "description": "This course is designed to educate all employees on the critical issue of preventing sexual harassment in the workplace. It provides a detailed examination of the Sexual Harassment of Women at Workplace (Prevention, Prohibition and Redressal) Act, 2013. The content addresses the importance of creating a safe, respectful, and professional environment for all, which is fundamental to organizational health and employee well-being. Key learning areas include a clear definition of sexual harassment with real-world examples, the distinction between 'quid pro quo' and a 'hostile work environment', and the legal obligations placed upon employers. Learners will gain a thorough understanding of the complaint mechanism, including the formation and functions of the Internal Complaints Committee (ICC), the step-by-step inquiry process, and the potential penalties for non-compliance. By completing this course, participants will be equipped to identify inappropriate behavior, understand their rights and duties, and contribute to a culture of zero tolerance for sexual harassment, ensuring a legally compliant and secure workplace.",
    "creator": "ISTM ISTM",
    "source": "Institute of Secretariat Training and Management",
